From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:20:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/47] cine(region): board-end blend view slerps from its
 blend-start direction

The 08->09 deck corners swing the Landing A view by up to 70 deg in the last
17 m; slerping from the moving lens view made the angle to the board camera go
17.3 -> 25.8 -> 2.0 -> 4.7 -> 0 deg. The view now slerps from the lens view at
the blend start, so the angle falls strictly ((1-e)*theta0). Position (C1 from
the moving lens) and FOV are unchanged. Max turn: meadow 4.49 -> 1.94 deg/s,
skycity 6.72 -> 1.77 deg/s; turn-rate jump at the hand-off 0.

test-region-landing-hook now checks cumulative monotonicity of FOV and view
angle over the whole blend, no camera back-up (velocity 0.5 s apart never
reverses), position drift-away <= 1 m, hand-off turn-rate jump <= 2 deg/s.
